// PRE-EXISTING wrong value, surfaced by the aug08e soak (hz1 generate,
// on 59f887ac). Deterministic 3/3, and DEEP: it diverges identically on
// every archived campaign binary reachable on hz1 — aug08c (fb622f09),
// aug08b, aug07a, aug06i (0174c8a2, pre-review-arc), aug06g, aug06e,
// aug06a, aug05k, aug05d. It predates the strict-select rule, the
// scrutinee ride, and the whole 08-07 review-fix arc; the aug08a map::
// and dynamic-module generator vocabulary is what finally reached it.
// Reproduces on aea9910d.
//
//   interp: [0:true, 1:true]
//   jit:    [0:true, 1:false]   <- epoch 1 value is the PRE-WRITE k0
//
// Kept here because campaign dirs live under ~/tmp, which is tmpfs on
// every box in the fleet — a reboot loses the only copy.
//
// Untriaged. Reduced from 2213 to 490 bytes by the minimizer (490
// checks — it dropped the dynamic module and the map::len scrutinee
// outright), then by hand to the floor below. The reduction facts,
// which are the useful part:
//
//   - `*v3 <- true` writes m0::k0 through a reference. At epoch 1 the
//     scrutinee (`true`) does not change; only the guard's k0 does.
//     The interp re-matches, selects arm 1, and m0::f1 returns the NEW
//     k0. The JIT selects arm 1 too — it fires — but f1 hands back the
//     stale false.
//   - BOTH halves are load-bearing, each verified by an AGREEing probe:
//       * arm body reading `m0::k0` DIRECTLY instead of through f1
//         agrees, so the guard sees the write correctly — it is the
//         CALLEE's read that is stale;
//       * a wildcard arm (`select true { v4 => m0::f1(u8:2) }`) or the
//         bare call with no select at all agrees, so the call alone is
//         fine — it needs the guard-driven becoming-selected dispatch.
//   - The MODULE BOUNDARY is load-bearing: the same program with k0/f1
//     as ordinary block-local lets (no m0) agrees.
//
// So: a becoming-selected arm dispatches a cross-module callee whose
// body reads a module-level binding written this cycle through a `&`,
// and the callee reads the pre-write value while the guard beside it
// reads the post-write one.
//
// bisect: fusion/JIT bug (interp != jit)
// interp: Trace([0:true 1:true])
// jit:    Trace([0:true 1:false])
// minimized:
{let v3 = &m0::k0; *v3 <- true; select true {v4 if m0::k0 => m0::f1(u8:2), v4 => true}}
// file-v1: m0.gxi
val k0: bool;
val f1: fn(a0: u8) -> bool;
// file-v1: m0.gx
let k0: bool = false;
let f1 = |v3: u8| -> bool k0
